  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.3\n- Added BlazorVisibilityMonitor implementing IRealtimeLifecycleMonitor: monitors document.visibilitychange via IJSRuntime to disconnect the realtime stream when the tab is hidden and reconnect when visible.\n- Registered by UseBlazor() to replace the no-op IRealtimeLifecycleMonitor default.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.2\n- Added BlazorRemoteConfigHeadersInterceptor to strip browser-unsafe headers (X-Firebase-RC-Fetch-Type, X-Google-GFE-Can-Retry, X-Accept-Response-Streaming) that trigger CORS preflight failures.\n- Registered via UseBlazor() so the interceptor is only active when the Blazor integration is opted in.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.1\n- Initial release.\n- IJSRuntime-based IndexedDB and localStorage persistence for Remote Config containers, settings, and metadata.\n- UseBlazor() extension method on FirebaseRemoteConfigBuilder for service registration.\n- Replaces in-memory stores with persistent browser storage across all Blazor hosting models (WASM, Server, Hybrid, Auto).\n- Automatically configures FireForNet.Firebase.Installations.Blazor when the installation store is still the core in-memory default; explicit IInstallationStore overrides are preserved.\n- IndexedDB persistence is isolated per configured database name and falls back to localStorage when IndexedDB is unavailable or security-blocked.\n- No dependency on FireForNet.Firebase.RemoteConfig.Browser — uses IJSRuntime modules directly.",
